# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# mycelia is a framework. What you run it on is YOUR configuration.
#
# The rule: this repository holds the fundamentals — structure, conventions,
# schema, runners. It never holds an operator's estate, notes, or paths.
# Anything named *.local.* is configuration and stays on the machine.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Configuration: your estate, never committed ---------------------------
control/*.local.yaml
control/*.local.md
control/roots.local.yaml

# --- Vault content: your notes, never committed ----------------------------
# The PARA directories ship with only their README explaining what belongs
# inside. Everything the operator actually writes stays local.
00-inbox/*
10-projects/*
20-areas/*
30-resources/*
40-archive/*
daily/*
!00-inbox/README.md
!10-projects/README.md
!20-areas/README.md
!30-resources/README.md
!40-archive/README.md
!daily/README.md

# The Sunday feedback channel is personal by definition.
FEEDBACK.md

# --- Runtime noise ---------------------------------------------------------
logs/
*.log

# Obsidian per-machine UI state. app.json IS committed so the vault config is
# reproducible for anyone who clones this. Excluding everything else by default
# (rather than naming known-noisy files) means a new Obsidian version or plugin
# that adds another per-machine state file is caught automatically instead of
# showing up as untracked noise until someone notices and adds it here (#5).
.obsidian/*
!.obsidian/app.json

# Extracted archives
handoff/extracted/

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
